.TH DQL-FORMAT 1 "2026-07-19" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-format \- format/prettify DelightQL source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql format
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fISOURCE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formats DelightQL source and prints the result to stdout.
.I SOURCE
is either literal source code or a path to a file containing it; if it
names a readable file the file is formatted, otherwise the argument
itself is treated as source. If
.I SOURCE
is omitted, stdin is read.
.PP
The formatter changes whitespace and nothing else: the output is
token-for-token identical to the input, comments included, and ends
with a final newline. Input that does not parse cleanly is passed
through unchanged with a warning on stderr, and the exit status is 2
(see EXIT STATUS).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-style " BUNDLE"
Apply a named style bundle from the
.B sys::format.bundle
system table (see CONFIGURATION). An unknown bundle name refuses.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
Colored output:
.BR always ,
.B auto
(default: detect terminal; honors
.BR NO_COLOR ),
or
.BR never .
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted
Print nothing; exit 0 if the input is already formatted, 1 if it is
not, 2 if the formatter cannot determine (parse error or pass-through,
see EXIT STATUS). A missing final newline alone does not count as
unformatted, so a literal command-line
.I SOURCE
is not penalized. For CI enforcement.
.TP
.BI \-\-highlights " FILE"
Path to a highlights.scm file.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " FILE"
Path to a theme file.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Layout knobs resolve in three layers, later layers overriding
earlier: the frozen defaults (the
.B book
style), then the bundle selected with
.BR \-\-style ,
then a
.B .dql-format
file in the working directory overriding individual knobs. Every knob
governs whitespace only \(em no configuration can change a token.
.PP
The knob inventory is itself queryable data: the
.B sys::format.bundle
system table carries one row per named style, with one column per
knob; the
.B book
row is the frozen default style. NULL in a bundle column means the
knob is inherited from the defaults. List the styles and knobs with
.EX
$ dql query 'sys::format.bundle(*)'
.EE
.PP
A
.B .dql-format
line naming an unknown knob, or an unparsable value, is warned about
on stderr \(em a typo'd key never silently does nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The tri-state of the tool-formatter lineage (gofmt, rustfmt):
.TP
.B 0
success; with
.BR \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted ,
the input is already formatted.
.TP
.B 1
with
.BR \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted ,
the input is not formatted (reformatting would change it).
.TP
.B 2
cannot determine: the input does not parse (both modes), or the
formatter passed it through unverified (with
.BR \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted ;
see PASS-THROUGH).
.SH PASS-THROUGH
Constructs the formatter does not yet handle are passed through
byte-for-byte rather than risk corrupting code \(em but loudly: a
warning on stderr names the first unhandled construct
(\(dqformatter does not yet handle node 'pipe_operator'\(dq), and
.B \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted
exits 2 (\(dqcannot determine\(dq), never 0, so a CI gate can
distinguish a formatter gap from verified-formatted code. The same
applies when the formatter discards its own work because the output's
token stream diverged from the input's.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ dql format 'a(*),b(*),a.id=b.id'
a(*), b(*), a.id = b.id
$ dql format query.dql
$ dql format --fail-if-not-formatted query.dql || echo needs formatting
.EE
.SH BUGS
Formatter coverage is incomplete: pipes
.RB ( |> ),
group-pipes
.RB ( ~> ),
and anonymous tables
.RB ( _(1,2;3,4) )
currently pass through (loudly \(em see PASS-THROUGH) instead of
being formatted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-query (1)
